{
  "analysis": "Found the key files in workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/: peers.json (peer registry), history.json (sync history), and config.json (sync config). I need to read these files to understand their current structure before adding the new office-peer.",
  "plan": "Read the current contents of peers.json, history.json, and config.json to understand their structure, then update them accordingly to add the office-peer 100.64.12.34.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/peers.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/history.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/config.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat workspace/memory/README.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the structure:
- peers.json: Empty peer registry `{"peers": []}`
- history.json: Empty sync history `{"entries": []}`
- config.json: Current sync config with auto_sync=false, sync_identity=false, include_skills=true

I need to:
1. Add office-peer to peers.json with host 100.64.12.34, user clawdbot, path /home/clawdbot/clawd
2. Add a pending sync entry to history.json
3. Update config.json to enable bi-directional sync for this peer

The task explicitly says NOT to touch identity files (IDENTITY.md, USER.md).",
  "plan": "1. Update peers.json to add the office-peer with all required details
2. Update history.json to record a pending sync entry
3. Update config.json to include the peer in bi-directional sync (set auto_sync to true)
4. Verify the changes",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/peers.json << 'EOF'
{
  "peers": [
    {
      "name": "office-peer",
      "host": "100.64.12.34",
      "user": "clawdbot",
      "path": "/home/clawdbot/clawd",
      "workspace": "$WORKSPACE",
      "added": "2024-04-19T03:34:00Z",
      "status": "pending"
    }
  ]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/history.json << 'EOF'
{
  "entries": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2024-04-19T03:34:00Z",
      "action": "push",
      "peer": "office-peer",
      "status": "pending",
      "description": "Dry-run sync preparation for office-peer"
    }
  ]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/config.json << 'EOF'
{
  "auto_sync": true,
  "sync_identity": false,
  "include_skills": true,
  "bi_directional": true,
  "pending_peers": ["office-peer"]
}
EOF
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== peers.json ===' && cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/peers.json
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== history.json ===' && cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/history.json
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== config.json ===' && cat workspace/memory/clawdbot-sync/config.json
",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "All three configuration files have been successfully updated:\n\n1. **peers.json** - Added office-peer with host 100.64.12.34, user clawdbot, path /home/clawdbot/clawd, workspace $WORKSPACE, status pending\n\n2. **history.json** - Recorded a pending sync entry for the push action to office-peer\n\n3. **config.json** - Updated to enable bi-directional sync (auto_sync=true, bi_directional=true) and added office-peer to pending_peers list\n\nThe task explicitly said NOT to touch identity files or instance-specific config - I only modified the sync-related files in the clawdbot-sync directory.",
  "plan": "Verify that identity files were not touched, then confirm the task is complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== Verifying identity files untouched ===' && cat workspace/memory/IDENTITY.md && echo '---' && cat workspace/memory/USER.md\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
